    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Read Me\n\n### Purpose\nGenerates a six-digit OTP, stores it in Redis, and sends it to the user's email for session verification.\n\n### Workflow Inputs\n| Input | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `session_id` | Unique session identifier |\n| `email` | Recipient's email address |\n| `TTL` | OTP expiration time in seconds |\n| `cooldown` | Optional resend cooldown in seconds (default: 60) |\n\n### Workflow Process\n1. **Generate Redis Keys** – Creates separate keys for the OTP and resend cooldown using the session ID and email.\n2. **Retrieve Existing OTP** – Checks Redis for an existing OTP record and parses its data.\n3. **Check Resend Eligibility** – Allows a new OTP if none exists or the resend count is below the configured maximum (3).\n4. **Check Cooldown** – Uses Redis `SET NX` to prevent repeated OTP requests during the cooldown period.\n5. **Generate OTP** – Uses the Crypto node to generate cryptographically secure random hexadecimal data, converted into a six-digit OTP.\n6. **Store OTP** – Saves the OTP, mismatch counter, and resend counter in Redis with the configured expiration time.\n7. **Send Email** – Sends the OTP to the recipient's email address.\n8. **Return Result** – Returns the appropriate status and message.\n\n### Redis Data\n**OTP Key:**\n`otp:{session_id}:{email}`\n\nStores:\n- `otp` – Six-digit verification code\n- `mismatch_count` – Failed verification attempts\n- `resend_count` – Number of OTP resends\n\n**Cooldown Key:**\n`otp:cooldown:{session_id}:{email}`\n\nTemporarily prevents repeated OTP requests.\n\n### Possible Responses\n| Status | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `OTP_SENT` | OTP generated and sent successfully |\n| `OTP_RESEND_COOLDOWN` | User must wait before requesting another OTP |\n| `OTP_MAX_RESEND_REACHED` | Maximum resend limit reached |\n\n### Configuration\n- Maximum resends: 3\n- OTP expiration: Configurable through `TTL`",
        "height": 1104,
        "width": 976,
        "color": 4
      },
